  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

  French translation of values/strings.xml.

  Placeholders are POSITIONAL (%1$s / %1$d) and keep their numbers.
  Apostrophes and quotation marks are written RAW: Compose Multiplatform only
  unescapes \uXXXX, \n, \t and \\, so a backslash would reach the UI.
  "LatentJam" and "SMART" are names and stay untranslated.

  Terminology follows real players (Spotify, Deezer, Apple Music):
  morceau, file d’attente, lecture aléatoire, playlist, bibliothèque.
  The app addresses the user with vous.
  French typography: guillemets «  » enclose a narrow no-break space (U+202F)
  on each side, ? is preceded by U+202F and : by a no-break space (U+00A0).
  Those characters are literal here, not escapes.
  Note: French CLDR puts 0 in the "one" category, which is why the singular
  reads correctly for both 0 and 1.
-->
